{=============================================================================
  SIHI pump simulation from dimensionless polynomials
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0240
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Example simulation of a SIHI pump. The head and absorbed-power
  coefficients are cubics of the flow coefficient, as written in the
  original equation window. The affinity-law definitions return the
  pressure rise and the shaft power at the stated diameter and speed.
  Water enters only through the suction density. The volume flow is the
  stored solution, 0.00508 m^3/s. The original brace comment
  V_dot_p = 0.00211 is not an equation.

  Inputs : volume flow, impeller diameter, speed, suction temperature
           and pressure
  Outputs: pressure rise, shaft power, epsilon_s
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J;
           speed kept in rev/min (omega in rad/s)
  Source : Felipe Trebilcock, Laborelec toolkit 2002 - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"!Polynomials for the dimensionless coefficients"
psi_p = 0.06593 + 193.982*phi_p - 2.68298E6*phi_p^2 + 2.14012E9*phi_p^3    "head coefficient [-]"
Lambda_p = 0.000005387 + 0.07254*phi_p - 91.0212*phi_p^2 + 42483*phi_p^3    "absorbed-power coefficient [-]"
epsilon_s_p = (psi_p*phi_p)/lambda_p    "epsilon_s = psi*phi/lambda [-], as in the original"

"!Affinity-law definitions"
psi_p = DELTAP_p/(rho_su_p*omega_p^2*D_p^2)    "head coefficient from the pressure rise [-]"
phi_p = V_dot_p/(D_p^3*omega_p)    "flow coefficient [-]"
Lambda_p = W_dot_shaft_p/(D_p^5*omega_p^3*rho_su_p)    "absorbed-power coefficient [-]"

"The original comment says the catalogue data for the polynomial identification belong in the parametric table. They are not equations of this window."

"!Suction state"
rho_su_p = DENSITY(Water, T=T_w_su_p, P=P_w_su_p)    "suction density [kg/m^3]"

"!Catalogue data and inputs"
D_p = 0.50    "impeller diameter [m]"
rpm_p = 2900    "rotational speed [rev/min]; original annotation [rev/m]"
omega_p = (rpm_p*2*pi)/60    "angular speed [rad/s]"
T_w_su_p = 20    "suction temperature [°C]"
P_w_su_p = 101300    "suction pressure [Pa]; 101.3 kPa in the original"
g = 9.81    "gravitational acceleration [m/s^2], as in the original"
V_dot_p = 0.00508    "volume flow rate [m^3/s]; stored solution. The original brace comment lists 0.00211 and is not an equation"
